// Plan 55 Ф.2 — negative: match arms возвращают несовместимые типы.
// `Some(v) => v` (int) и `None => "str"` — type-check error.

module neg.f2_negative_match_arm_type_mismatch


// EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR E7301
//
// STRENGTHENED 2026-09-05 (registry #959). This fixture used to expect the C
// COMPILER to catch the mismatch -- its marker matched the word "initializing"
// in a C diagnostic, which is to say it documented that Nova did NOT catch a
// match-arm type mismatch at all. Since the return position is checked (#959),
// Nova refuses it itself, in the user's own file, with a name.
//
// A strengthening, not a weakening: D405's amendment of 2026-09-04, point 4,
// says in as many words that leaning on the C compiler is NOT acceptance for
// this class -- "checker, not C". Ten other fixtures still lean that way; they
// are the same debt and not this wave's business.
//
// (The old marker's name is deliberately NOT spelled out above: the runner
// reads markers out of the first lines, and a marker quoted in prose is a
// marker as far as it is concerned.)
fn bad(opt Option[int]) -> int {
    match opt {
        // nova:expect E7301 -- #959: a str leaves through a match arm of a function declared `-> int`
        Some(v) => v
        None    => "not an int"     // type mismatch
    }
}
